+# Week 12 results, figures and examples
+
+**November 1, 2026: Steps 2 and 3 are complete.** The existing Weeks 9–11 evidence
+is consolidated under the unchanged [scope](WEEK12_SCOPE.md) and
+[report outline](WEEK12_REPORT_OUTLINE.md).
+
+- [Consolidated results and statistics](evaluation/week12-results-v1/RESULTS.md):
+  rates, paired intervals, factorial effects, latency, cost and stopping decisions.
+- [Final figure and example gallery](evaluation/week12-results-v1/gallery.html):
+  five architecture/statistical figures in PNG, SVG and PDF, four main qualitative
+  panels, and fourteen retained examples with provenance.
+- [Figure captions and exports](evaluation/week12-results-v1/CAPTIONS.md) and
+  [qualitative interpretations](evaluation/week12-results-v1/QUALITATIVE.md).
+- [Complete tables](evaluation/week12-results-v1/tables/TABLES.md) and
+  [machine-readable results](evaluation/week12-results-v1/consolidated.json).
+- [Package inventory and verification](evaluation/week12-results-v1/README.md).
+
+The analysis independently reproduces the retained bootstrap results and checks
+counts, prediction scores and timing quantiles: 2,210 numerical checks pass.
+The table exports contain 29 success-rate rows, 36 contrasts, 22 latency rows,
+7 training-cost entries and 7 revised event-forecasting summaries. Distinct
+panels, training budgets and exploratory screens remain separate.
+
+The five-arm study establishes no overall coupling benefit. The event study
+establishes no additional RLVR benefit. Formal adaptive routing fails its
+performance gates, and later exploratory follow-ups establish no replacement
+for original M4. M4 remains the Week 11 reference, not an overall Week 9 winner.
+
+Qualitative material includes eight deterministically selected formal outcome
+classes, three prior physical-mechanism inspections and three weak-label event
+forecasts. Image bytes are unchanged from prior media receipts. Selected
+examples illustrate behavior; they do not measure its frequency or establish
+independent label truth.
+
+No model calls, training, rollouts or new labeling were performed. Verification
+covers retained local evidence, not a new remote raw-recording/checkpoint audit.
+Full-10K/test remain locked. [Steps 4–6](WEEK12_STATUS.md) remain unstarted.
